  "description": "Account groups and accounts for a small trading or service business in Malaysia, grouped so each group totals what is under it. Codes, names and groups are a starting point: rename or deactivate what the business does not use.",
  "notes": [
    "Sales tax and service tax have separate accounts because the two are accounted differently. Use them only if the business is registered and its supplies are taxable; deactivate them otherwise. Which basis applies to a business needs client-specific advice.",
    "Employee and employer shares of EPF, SOCSO and EIS have separate payable accounts, and employer contributions have separate expense accounts. Contribution rates and bases are not part of any account and change over time.",
    "Retained earnings is marked for the year-end close. Opening balances are not included; bring them in as part of converting an existing business."
  ],
